-## Implemented model and covariance semantics
-
-* State: 12 coordinates per moving body, translation-first left SE(3) errors,
-  spatial twist, right/body pose process noise, full F/G and inter-body blocks.
-  Initial pose gauge coordinates are eliminated. The static world has no twist.
-* Process: explicit per-interval discrete covariance or Van Loan discretization
-  of declared continuous left-error diffusion. Continuous diffusion is converted
-  to equivalent D1 right-pose noise at the original prior reference and frozen
-  as the specified discrete model; this is not an exact nonlinear diffusion law.
-  Position/twist cross terms are retained, and Q is added only once.
-* Map: every valid source depth from the complete sequence proposes a finite
-  oriented surfel with component-conditioned canonical position/appearance.
-  Source observations initialize proposals only. Raw source rays enter the same
-  likelihood exactly once, including links to earlier/nonconsecutive frames.
-* Measurement: normalized RGB-D first-hit mixture with finite polygon/pixel
-  overlap, correct no-return mass and normalized background return density.
-  Full analytic scores include coverage, empty rays, depth and any declared
-  depth-dependent covariance. There is no ICP or additional reprojection loss.
-* Discrete inference: `q(z)=sum_r w_r delta(z-z_r)`, a deterministic finite-support
-  categorical **variational** distribution over complete coupled scenes.
-  The full log likelihood is evaluated per scene before averaging. This is not
-  a mean-existence renderer or an exact unrestricted posterior. The support is
-  fixed/checkpointed and restrictive: correlations/probabilities outside that
-  support are unrepresented, and arbitrary true segmentation is not guaranteed.
-* Stage A runs an actual fixed-prediction-prior conditional IEKF and backward
-  RTS; all chart transports are exported. Stage B refines shared canonical
-  geometry at frozen motion. Joint refinement applies the complete sparse
-  trajectory/map operator. Each accepted stage uses the same all-ray ELBO.
-* Local factor JVP/VJP actions and disk-backed bounded chunks retain all ray
-  cross-point/cross-body information. Only explicitly independent map **prior**
-  blocks use repeated block algebra. Matrix-free Schur solves never approximate
-  a coupled map block by its diagonal. Jacobi is a preconditioner only.
-* Gaussian covariance uses an undamped **empirical full-score information
-  approximation** at fixed variational q. It is not an exact observed-Hessian
-  Laplace covariance or a multimodal posterior variance. LM damping affects
-  directions only. Selected joint inverse blocks come from checked sparse solves;
-  conditional filtering/RTS and motion-given-map covariance are labeled separately.
-* Fixed calibration, conditional unfiltered-ray independence and independent
-  canonical hypothesis priors are explicit assumptions. Uncertain extrinsics
-  are not spuriously added independently to points: unsupported shared nuisance
-  configurations fail explicitly. Improper/singular priors requiring additional
-  deterministic constraints are rejected rather than replaced by giant variances
-  or jitter. Nonsmooth coverage/depth-order boundaries can cause a reported stall.
-
